* Upgrade the system
@code bash
sudo pacman -Syu
@end
`-yy` forces a database refresh; `-uu` also allows downgrades. Use them for a specific recovery or repository change, not routine updates.

* Install while upgrading the system
@code bash
sudo pacman -Syu package
@end

* Uninstall with unused dependencies
@code bash
sudo pacman -Rs package
@end

* Remove cached packages that are no longer installed
@code bash
sudo pacman -Sc
@end

* Remove all cached packages
@code bash
sudo pacman -Scc
@end
This also removes cached versions that could otherwise be reinstalled without downloading.

* List updates known to the local package database
@code bash
pacman -Qu
@end
This does not refresh repository metadata. Avoid `pacman -Sy package`, which can cause a partial upgrade.

Reference: {https://man.archlinux.org/man/pacman.8.en}[pacman manual].
